# Safety net for manual `docker build` invocations.
# The build script (docker_build_push.sh) assembles the build context from
# git-tracked files; the model data is downloaded from Zenodo during the build.
# These rules are a secondary safeguard only.

# Version control and IDE
.git/
.history/
.Rproj.user/
.vscode/
.claude/

# Sensitive and non-essential directories
secure_data/
docker_setup/
# ...except the build-time Zenodo data-download helper, which the Dockerfile runs
!docker_setup/download_zenodo_data.R
# ...and entrypoint.sh, which the model Dockerfile re-copies from the CODE overlay
# ("Refresh the container ENTRYPOINT", added 2026-07-02) so an entrypoint fix does
# not stay dormant until the next ~33GB data rebuild. Without this negation the
# COPY-method build has no docker_setup/ in its context and dies at that step with
# `cp: cannot stat '/IMPACTncd_England/docker_setup/entrypoint.sh'`. The git-clone
# and commit-fallback paths never noticed: neither filters through .dockerignore.
!docker_setup/entrypoint.sh
documents/
debugging_info/
auxil/
validation/
validation_internal/

# Scenario drivers and their sim_design YAMLs are NOT shipped in the image.
# /IMPACTncd_England/scenarios is where setup_user_docker_env.sh -ScenariosDir
# bind-mounts the USER's own scenarios folder, so a baked copy is shadowed
# whenever it would be used. This entry is what keeps them out of the COPY-method
# build context; the git-clone method prunes them inside Dockerfile.IMPACTncdENGL
# (same RUN as the clone, so they never reach a layer), and that Dockerfile also
# asserts the folder ships empty.
scenarios/

# Runtime directories (not in git)
outputs/
synthpop/

# Python virtual environment
.venv/

# R session files
.Rhistory
.RData
